---
title: Argentine Beef Tenderloin with Malbec Sauce
course: main
cuisine: argentine
servings: 2
time_active: 25
time_total: 45
leftovers: poor
tags: [date-night]
pairs: [smoked-paprika-sweet-potatoes, chimichurri-quinoa-salad]
---

> Start the sweet potatoes and quinoa first, then sear the steaks while they cook.

Season @beef tenderloin steaks{2}(4 to 6 oz each, about 1 inch thick) with @salt and @black pepper{}. Let them sit at room temperature while you prep.

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #cast iron skillet{} over high heat until shimmering. Sear the steaks ~{3-4%minutes} per side for medium-rare (135°F). Move to a plate, tent with foil, and rest.

== Malbec Sauce ==

Lower the heat to medium. Add @butter{1%tbsp} and @shallot{1}(minced) and cook until soft, ~{2%minutes}.

Pour in @red wine{1/2%cup}(preferably Malbec), scraping up the browned bits. Simmer until reduced by half, ~{4-5%minutes}.

Add @beef broth{1/4%cup}, @balsamic vinegar{1/2%tsp}, and @fresh rosemary{1/2%tsp}(chopped, or 1/4 tsp dried). Simmer ~{3%minutes}.

For a thicker sauce, stir in @?cornstarch{1/2%tsp} mixed with 1 tbsp water and cook ~{1%minute}. Season to taste.

Slice the steaks against the grain and spoon the sauce over.
